p.src:
The position derivative of the Lagrangian is $\frac{\partial L}{\partial x}
=
\frac{\partial\phi}{\partial x}
\sqrt{1-\dot x^2}.$ Keeping the sign fixed by the action [eq:sr4-coupled-action], the Euler–Lagrange equation is therefore $\boxed{
\frac{d}{dt}
\left[
(m-\phi)
\frac{\dot x}{\sqrt{1-\dot x^2}}
\right]
=
\frac{\partial\phi}{\partial x}
\sqrt{1-\dot x^2}
}.$

